_refine.details                                  
;THE PAPER CITED ON THE *JRNL* RECORDS ABOVE DISCUSSES THE
QUESTION AS TO WHETHER THE PEPTIDE BOND BETWEEN GLY 95 AND
GLY 96 IS IN THE CIS OR THE TRANS CONFORMATION.
A DISORDERED MODEL IN WHICH THIS PEPTIDE EXISTS IN BOTH
CONFORMERS CANNOT BE RULED OUT.  IN THIS ENTRY, HOWEVER,
ONLY COORDINATES CORRESPONDING TO THE TRANS CONFORMATION
ARE PROVIDED.

RESIDUES PRO 21 - LEU 24 ARE WEAK.  THERE IS UNINTERPRETED
DENSITY ASSOCIATED WITH THE SIDE CHAIN OF PHE 31.  RESIDUES
GLY 95 - GLY 96 ARE PARTIALLY DISORDERED.  VAL 10, GLU 120,
ASP 122, AND ASP 127 HAVE DISORDERED SIDE CHAINS.  THE SIDE
CHAIN OF LEU 28, IN THE SUBSTRATE BINDING SITE, APPEARS TO
BE PARTIALLY DISORDERED.
;
