loop_
_atom_sites_footnote.id 
_atom_sites_footnote.text 
1 
;RESIDUES PRO 21 - LEU 24 ARE WEAK.  THERE IS UNINTERPRETED DENSITY ASSOCIATED WITH THE SIDE CHAIN OF PHE 31.  RESIDUES 95 - 96 ARE PARTIALLY DISORDERED.  VAL 10, GLU 120, ASP 122, AND ASP 127 HAVE DISORDERED SIDE CHAINS.  THE SIDE CHAIN OF LEU 28, IN THE SUBSTRATE BINDING SITE, APPEARS TO BE PARTIALLY DISORDERED.
;
2 
;THE IDENTITY OF IONS 501 THROUGH 503 IS NOT DETERMINED. THEY HAVE TENATIVELY BEEN ASSIGNED AS CHLORINE IONS BASED ON THEIR ELECTRON DENSITY, THE BINDING ENVIRONMENT, AND THE BELIEF THAT CHLORIDE IS THE ONLY NEGATIVELY-CHARGED MONO-ATOMIC ION PRESENT IN THE CRYSTALLIZATION MIXTURE.
;
# 
